import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="Who I am and how this devlog works.">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    Hi, I'm Mario, from Spain. My day job is Jira administration, and game development is what I'm passionate
    about: I started teaching myself to code many years ago, in C#, while learning Unity.
  </p>
  <p>
    Right now my goal is to find out the real potential of AI in today's development environments.
  </p>
  <p>Thanks for visiting my small space on the internet!</p>

  <h2>What I'm doing right now</h2>
  <p>
    Learning by building. NihonWorld is the main project, and around it I'm practising the stuff that real teams
    use: architecture decision records, Jira and Confluence, CI, and reviews that end in a clear READY or NOT READY.
  </p>

  <h2>How I work with AI</h2>
  <p>
    Think of the agents as different workers, each one with their own field. One writes code, another reviews it,
    another checks the security side. They audit each other, so one of them can't greenlight something that isn't
    properly tested. They propose; I decide every point, every merge and every closed ticket.
  </p>

  <h2>How this site works</h2>
  <p>
    Built with Astro and hosted on GitHub Pages. Every entry goes through a pull request, and merging it is my
    approval. Drafts are written with help from AI assistants, then reviewed and edited by me.
  </p>
</Base>
